<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>The Crawl Price Index — what the web charges AI to read it</title>
<meta name="description" content="A weekly, independent measure of what the web charges AI crawlers: block rates, the one observed per-crawl price, and where the pay-per-crawl market is heading.">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27 viewBox=%270 0 32 32%27%3E%3Crect width=%2732%27 height=%2732%27 fill=%27%23FBFAF8%27/%3E%3Crect x=%276%27 y=%2714%27 width=%2720%27 height=%274%27 fill=%27%231C5D4A%27/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,300&family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/theme.css">
<style>
.bignum{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(52px,9vw,104px);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:var(--signal)}
.bignum .u{font-size:.28em;color:var(--dim);letter-spacing:0}
.nprice{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:13px;color:var(--amber);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.04em}
.trend-svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin-top:6px;max-width:100%}
.trend-legend{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim)}
.trend-legend b{display:inline-block;width:22px;height:2px;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}
.brow2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px 1fr 52px;gap:12px;align-items:center;font-size:13.5px;padding:4px 0}
.brow2 .nm{white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.brk{height:13px;background:var(--sand);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden}
.brk>span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--signal);width:0;transition:width .7s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.brow2 .pc{text-align:right;color:var(--dim);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.postgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:6px}
.postcell{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:16px;background:var(--sand);min-width:0}
.postcell.hi{border-left:3px solid var(--signal)}
.postcell .pn{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:30px;color:var(--fg)}
.postcell.hi .pn{color:var(--signal)}
.postcell .pt{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--fg);font-weight:600;margin-top:2px}
.postcell .pd{font-size:12px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4}
.calc-out{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(34px,6vw,60px);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--signal);margin:2px 0}
.slider{margin:16px 0}
.slider label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13.5px;margin-bottom:8px;gap:10px}
.slider label b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--signal);font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}
.slider input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--signal)}
.assume{font-size:12px;color:var(--dim);line-height:1.5;margin-top:14px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.tick{display:flex;gap:10px;overflow-x:auto;padding:4px 0 2px;margin-top:10px}
.tick .ti{flex:0 0 auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:8px 12px;font-size:12.5px;background:#fff;white-space:nowrap}
.tick .ti b{color:var(--fg)}
.tick .ti .tg{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;margin-right:6px}
.tg.PRICED{color:var(--signal)} .tg.GATED{color:var(--amber)} .tg.LICENSING{color:var(--blue)} .tg.FREE{color:var(--dim)}
.subrow-3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin-top:16px}
.subrow-2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin-top:14px}
.subpanel{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:14px;background:var(--sand)}
.subpanel.hi{border-left:3px solid var(--signal)}
.subpanel .sublabel{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--signal);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px}
.slidernote{font-size:11px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4}
@media(max-width:720px){.subrow-3,.subrow-2{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
@media(max-width:640px){.postgrid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.brow2{grid-template-columns:110px 1fr 44px}}
</style>
</head>
<body class="prose">
<div class="masthead"><div class="wrap">
  <a class="mark" href="/">The Crawl Price Index<b>.</b></a>
  <nav class="navmid">
    <a class="lnk" href="/why">Why it matters</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/check">Check a domain</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/explore">Explore data</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/methodology">Method</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/about">About</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="navend">
    <a class="btn ghostbox" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com">Sign in</a>
    <a class="btn" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com/dashboard.html#account">Full dataset &mdash; &euro;49/mo</a>
  </div>
</div></div>

<div class="page-open"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Independent &middot; at least weekly &middot; edition of <span id="asof-eyebrow">&mdash;</span></p>
  <h1>What the web charges <em>AI</em> to read it.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every edition we read the declared crawler policy of a ranked <span id="lede-topn">50,000</span>-domain frame, one domain at a time, and write down what each tells <b>18 named AI crawlers</b>. Independent, weekly, and denominator-first &mdash; every figure here states what it is a share of.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="wrap"><div class="panels">

  <section class="panel wide" id="v2-census">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">The census</span></div>
    <h2>What we count, and what we count it against.</h2>
    <p>Every edition we read the <code>robots.txt</code> of a ranked 50,000-domain frame and record what each domain declares to <b>18 named AI crawlers</b>: blocked, allowed, partial, no instruction, or no file at all. Rates are quoted against the domains that actually serve a readable file &mdash; never against &ldquo;the web&rdquo;.</p>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;margin-top:18px" id="v2-census-nums">
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)"><span id="v2-parsed">&mdash;</span></div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">domains serving a readable robots.txt</div></div>
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)">18</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">AI crawlers tracked by name</div></div>
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)"><span id="v2-frame">&mdash;</span></div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">domains in the ranked frame</div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:14px" id="v2-frameprov">&nbsp;</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel wide">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Training versus traffic</span></div>
    <h2>Sites treat the crawler that <em>trains</em> differently from the one that <em>sends a reader</em>.</h2>
    <p>This is the most economically loaded thing in the dataset, and it does not show up in a headline block rate. A crawler that ingests your work to train a model and a crawler that might send you a visitor are different propositions &mdash; and domains that draw a line overwhelmingly draw it in one direction.</p>
    <div id="v2-asym" class="dvtri"></div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px">Declared robots.txt policy only. Role tags describe each crawler&rsquo;s stated function; this is not evidence of intent, and not proof any crawler was denied.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">What changed this week</span></div>
    <h2>Policy is not settled.</h2>
    <div id="v2-changes"></div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px">One edition-over-edition comparison, not a trend. Domains entering or leaving the frame are excluded, so frame churn is never counted as a policy change.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Declared versus enforced</span></div>
    <h2>What a site says and what its front door does.</h2>
    <div id="v2-reach"></div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px">A popularity ranking lists domains, not working websites. We census the frame itself so every rate we publish has an honest denominator &mdash; and we keep declared policy and enforced access as separate measurements.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel wide">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">The machine market</span></div>
    <h2>Machines already pay each other. Almost none of it touches the web you read.</h2>
    <p>Alongside the census we capture a public registry of endpoints advertising a price a machine can pay directly, settled in stablecoin. It is a real, working market &mdash; and it is almost entirely developer APIs and tools rather than the sites people visit.</p>
    <div id="v2-bazaar" class="dvsplit"></div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px">Advertised, opt-in acceptance in a public registry &mdash; never transactions, volume or revenue. This is a stablecoin rail, distinct from Cloudflare pay-per-crawl, though both return HTTP 402.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel wide">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">The wall is rising</span></div>
    <h2>Block rates, every edition since the baseline.</h2>
    <p>Each edition we record the declared block rate for every tracked crawler and archive it. The series is short &mdash; five editions &mdash; so this chart shows movement between editions, not a trend, and we do not describe it as one anywhere on this site. The archive is the part a later entrant cannot reconstruct: a week not measured is gone.</p>
    <div style="position:relative">
      <svg class="trend-svg" id="trend" viewBox="0 0 800 260" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" aria-label="Block rate trend"></svg>
      <div id="trend-tip" style="position:absolute;display:none;pointer-events:none;background:var(--fg);color:#fff;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12px;padding:6px 9px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;z-index:20"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="trend-legend" id="trend-legend"></div>
    <p style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px;line-height:1.5">This plots the <em>change</em> in each edition's block rate versus the one before, so a point below zero means that edition's rate ticked down, not that blocking reversed. Small dips (like 16 Aug) reflect coverage variation &mdash; each scan reaches a slightly different set of domains, so the reachable sample shifts a little edition to edition. The underlying level has risen across the series.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Who gets blocked</span></div>
    <h2>Not all crawlers are treated alike.</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:12px">Share of domains with a readable robots.txt that disallow each crawler. Training bots are walled harder than the search crawlers that send traffic back.</p>
    <div id="rates"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">How the door answers</span></div>
    <h2>Priced, gated, or blocked.</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:4px">When an identified AI crawler knocks, the response falls into a few distinct behaviours &mdash; measured on the wire this edition.</p>
    <div class="postgrid" id="posture"></div>
    <div class="tick" id="board"></div>
  </section>



  <section class="panel wide">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Coverage &amp; method</span></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:20px">
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)"><span id="f-parsed">&mdash;</span></div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">domains with a readable robots.txt</div></div>
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)"><span id="f-topn">&mdash;</span></div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">Tranco frame scanned</div></div>
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)"><span id="f-gpt">&mdash;</span>%</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">block GPTBot</div></div>
      <div style="min-width:0"><div class="bignum" style="font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,42px)">$<span id="f-price">&mdash;</span></div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:4px">highest observed price</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="source" style="margin-top:20px">Coverage is of domains that serve a readable robots.txt, not the raw list &mdash; unreachable domains are censused separately. Headline figures are free to cite with attribution. <a href="/methodology">Full methodology &rarr;</a></p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/check">Check any domain &mdash; free</a>
      <a class="ghost" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com/dashboard.html#account">Full dataset &mdash; &euro;49/mo</a>
      <a class="ghost" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com/dashboard.html#account">Single snapshot &mdash; &euro;29 one-off</a>
      <a class="ghost" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com">Explore the free edition</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel wide" id="weekly">
    <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">The Weekly Crawl &mdash; free</span></div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:36px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-top:8px">
      <p style="flex:1;min-width:300px;color:var(--dim);margin:0">One email a week: which domains changed their AI-crawler policy, the block-rate shifts, and the observed crawl prices. Free &mdash; and you get an instant data sample (the top-100 domains&rsquo; full rows) the moment you sign up.</p>
      <div style="flex:0 1 380px;min-width:280px">
        <form id="subform" onsubmit="return cpiSub(event)" style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <input id="subemail" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com" style="flex:1;min-width:200px;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#fff;color:var(--fg);font-size:14px;border-radius:2px">
          <button class="btn" type="submit">Get the weekly email</button>
        </form>
        <p id="submsg" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim);margin:10px 0 0;min-height:1em"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div></div>

<footer class="sitefoot"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="footlede">
    <h2>The market is being built now. The record starts <em>now</em> too.</h2>
    <p>A week that isn&rsquo;t measured is gone &mdash; no one can reconstruct it later, including us. Every edition is archived the day it is taken.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="footgrid">
    <div class="footcard">
      <div class="fk">Free</div>
